                                                                                
 Usage: opentide setup vscode [OPTIONS] [path]                                  
                                                                                
 Recommend the opentide extension and write snippets (deprecated). Default:     
 both.                                                                          
                                                                                
╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ --path         -C      <str>  Repository path [default: .]                   │
│ --settings                    Recommend the opentide extension in            │
│                               .vscode/extensions.json, and remove opentide's │
│                               yaml.schemas from .vscode/settings.json        │
│ --snippets                    Write object template snippets                 │
│ --no-merge                    Replace extensions.json instead of merging     │
│ --no-generate                 Do not run opentide generate first             │
│ --mcp                         Also write .vscode/mcp.json (same as setup mcp │
│                               --vscode)                                      │
│ --yes          -y             Accepted for symmetry with other setup         │
│                               subcommands; this command never prompts        │
│ --plan                        List the files each step would write, and      │
│                               write nothing                                  │
│ --help                        Show this message and exit.                    │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

 Examples
   $ opentide setup vscode --settings
